In 2005, she completed[ her] PM&[R] residency as[ chief] resident at Sinai Hospital (University of Maryland) in Baltimore[.] Dr. Bethea is also fellowship trained in interventional spine and joint pain management and worked for a neurosurgical practice for[ three] years before opening her own practice in Reidsville. In 2014 she moved[ that practice] to Greensboro.
Pl[ate]let-rich plasma treatment,[ a natural] procedure[ using the] patient�[�s own] blood, is one of the more rewarding services Dr. Bethea offers her patients. It is recommended for[ healing] damaged or injured tissues. PRP involves[ drawing] blood[ from a] patient, spinning[ it in a] centrif[uge], and[ extracting the] plasma and platelets from[ the whole] blood, which are injected back into[ the painful], injured areas,[ on] the same day.
